      "content": "Certainly, wealth inequality in the United States has notably increased due to a combination of factors. One major reason is the growth of high-paying jobs in technology and finance, often inaccessible to lower-wage workers. Changes in tax policies and benefit programs, such as the reduction of capital gains taxes and the weakening of union power, have also favored wealth accumulation among the higher-income groups. Deregulation and globalization have led to increased corporate profits while wage growth has lagged, further contributing to the disparity in wealth distribution. Lastly, disparities in education and healthcare access can exacerbate socio-economic divides and influence wealth accumulation. These factors together create a complex and interlinked picture of the reasons behind rising wealth inequality.",
